<title>MEXICO: Senate OKs new Banco de Mexico deputy governor.</title>
<headline>Senate OKs new Banco de Mexico deputy governor.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican Senate on Tuesday approved the nomination of Jose Sidaoui Dib as a new deputy governor of Banco de Mexico, replacing the retiring Ariel Buira, pro-government TV channel 24 Horas said.</p>
<p>Sidaoui, formerly deputy finance minister, was proposed for the job last week by President Ernesto Zedillo.</p>
<p>Analysts said his appointment was unlikely to affect current strict monetary policy.</p>
<p>-- Martin Langfield, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9558</p>
